-- title:
--   Drinfeld-chart reading of the j-finite chart algebra
-- statement:
--   Fix a prime $q$ and $M'\neq 0$ with $q\nmid M'$, and a prime $\ell$ with $\ell\equiv 11\pmod{12}$ and $\ell\mid M'$. Let $L$ be a field of characteristic zero, $\zeta\in L$ a primitive $q$-th root of unity admitting a ring embedding $\iota\colon L\to\mathbb C$ with $\iota(\zeta)=e^{2\pi i/q}$, let $H_1\le(\mathbb Z/q^2M')^\times$ be the intersection of the kernel of reduction to $(\mathbb Z/q)^\times$ with the kernel of reduction to $(\mathbb Z/\ell)^\times$, and let $K\subseteq\mathrm{LaurentSeries}(L)$ be the $L$-subfield generated by the image under coefficientwise base change of the $q$-expansion function field of $\Gamma_{H_1}(q^2M')$. Let $A$ be a henselian discrete valuation ring with fraction field $L$, algebraically closed residue field, $q$ in its maximal ideal, $\zeta$ in the image of $A$, uniformiser $\varpi$, and $\varpi_t\in A$ with $\varpi_t^{q^2-1}=q\cdot(\text{unit})$; assume $K$ is an $A$-algebra compatibly with $L$, and let $j\in K$, $j\neq 0$, have Laurent expansion the image of the classical $j$-series. Write $C=\mathrm{chartAlgFin}\,A\,K\,j$ for the integral closure of $A[j]$ in $K$. Let $y\subset C$ be a maximal ideal containing $\varpi$ and supersingular, in the sense that every ring homomorphism $\varphi$ from $C$ to an algebraically closed field of characteristic $q$ with kernel $y$ sends $j$ into $\mathrm{ssJSet}\,q$, i.e. every elliptic curve with $j$-invariant $\varphi(j)$ has no nonzero $q$-torsion point. Let $z$ be a point of the two-chart integral model $\mathfrak X=\mathrm{TwoChartIntegralModel}\,A\,K\,j$ (the pushout of the two affine charts) at which the germ of $\varpi$ pulled back from $\operatorname{Spec}A$ lies in the maximal ideal of the stalk, and let $y'\in\operatorname{Spec}C$ satisfy $\iota_{\mathrm{Fin}}(y')=z$, the same supersingularity condition, and $y'.\mathrm{asIdeal}=y$. Finally let a Drinfeld chart be given at $z$: a complete discrete valuation ring $W_1$, a ring map $\sigma_1\colon A\to W_1$ with $\mathfrak m_{W_1}=(\sigma_1\varpi)$, units $u_1,v_1$ and an element $f_1$ of $W_1[[X_0,X_1]]$ with $f_1\equiv X_0X_1^q-X_0^qX_1 \pmod{(X_0,X_1)^{q+2}}$, and a ring isomorphism $e_1$ from the $\mathfrak m$-adic completion of the stalk $\mathcal O_{\mathfrak X,z}$ onto $S=W_1[[X_0,X_1]]/(\sigma_1(\varpi_t^{q+1})v_1-f_1u_1)$ carrying the image of each $a\in A$ to the class of the constant $\sigma_1 a$. Let $\Psi\colon C\to S$ be the composite of the canonical map $C\to\mathcal O_{\mathfrak X,z}$ with completion and $e_1$, and $\mathfrak M=(\sigma_1\varpi,X_0,X_1)S$. The conclusion asserts: $\Psi^{-1}(\mathfrak M)=y$; for every $n$ and every $s\in S$ there is $a\in C$ with $\Psi(a)-s\in\mathfrak M^n$; $\Psi(a)=\sigma_1(a)$ as a constant for $a\in A$; $C=A+y$; $W_1=\sigma_1(A)+\mathfrak m_{W_1}$ and $\sigma_1^{-1}(\mathfrak m_{W_1})=\mathfrak m_A$; $\mathfrak M$ is maximal and is the only maximal ideal of $S$; and $S$ is flat as a $C$-module for the algebra structure given by $\Psi$.
--
--   This records the local reading, at a supersingular point of the integral model of the modular curve of level $H_1$, of the chart algebra against the Drinfeld local chart $W_1[[X_0,X_1]]/(\sigma_1(\varpi_t^{q+1})v_1-f_1u_1)$ of Katz–Mazur type: the comparison map is centred at the given maximal ideal, has dense image adically, matches constants, induces equality of residue fields, and is flat. It is the $\Gamma_1(\ell)$-guarded variant valid for all primes $q$, and feeds the blow-up chart analysis of the components and inertia action above a supersingular point.
